# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is git-ignored.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# The chat/vision model is NOT set here any more. It is a practice setting,
# stored in Postgres (app_settings) and changed at /settings, where it is picked
# from the live OpenRouter catalogue. Default: google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite.
# It should be vision-capable — the RAG ingester reads images with the fast model
# and falls back to this one when that model cannot see (no OCR engine either way).
# Embedding model for the knowledge base. OpenRouter serves it on the same key.
# Routed to Azure only (OpenRouter "Private": no training, no prompt retention).
OPENROUTER_EMBED_MODEL=openai/text-embedding-3-small
# --- Model roles -------------------------------------------------------------
# These are DEFAULTS. /settings overrides any of them per role in Postgres, so a
# model can be changed without a redeploy. Everything below is optional: with
# only the model at /settings chosen, every role uses it.
#
# A turn splits in two: READING (searching the practice's material, skimming what
# comes back, choosing the next file to open, extracting claims, pulling names out
# of a pasted list, transcribing a screenshot) and DECIDING (the answer, and every
# judgement in it). The reading is most of the calls and none of the output.
#
# The FAST role does the reading — including the agent's whole research loop, so
# it must call tools reliably; a model that answers in prose instead of searching
# is caught in code and the loop is run again on the reasoning model, which is
# slower and dearer than choosing a competent one here. Wants cheap and quick.
# Routed only to zero-retention providers (data_collection: deny).
OPENROUTER_ANALYSIS_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# The WEB role: one search of the open internet, only when the practice's own
# material does not cover the question, plus reading a page for a phone number.
# A search-grounded model belongs here.
# Defaults to OPENROUTER_MEDICATION_MODEL, then the analysis model.
# OPENROUTER_WEB_MODEL=perplexity/sonar
# The ACCURX role reads a pasted /accurx request against the practice's own
# routing pages and says where it goes. It is the only role whose answer is a
# judgement about a patient rather than material for one — and the only one that
# defaults to the FAST model rather than to the one chosen at /settings, so
# leaving this unset changes nothing. It can never make a message less urgent
# than the practice's own rules already did (lib/templates/accurx-route.mjs), so
# a better model here buys recall and nothing it could take away.
# OPENROUTER_ACCURX_MODEL=
# The SUPER SPEED role checks a message for patient details BEFORE it is sent,
# and stops it if there are any (lib/safety/patient-data.mjs). It is the only
# call in the app a reader waits on with nothing on the screen yet, so set it to
# the QUICKEST model available rather than the cleverest — it answers one closed
# question with one word. It defaults to the FAST model rather than to the one
# chosen at /settings, deliberately: a large careful model here would sit in
# front of every message anybody types.
# OPENROUTER_SUPER_SPEED_MODEL=
# There is no VISION role: images are read by the fast model, and by the model
# chosen at /settings when the fast one cannot.
# The Medication Check tool (app/api/medication) calls OpenRouter's web-search
# server tool to gather information from authoritative UK sources (NHS, BNF/NICE,
# eMC). Web search is billed per request by OpenRouter on top of the model tokens;
# results are cached in Postgres (the `medications` table) so each medicine and
# question is only fetched once.
# It uses its own model so it can pick one that reliably returns grounded JSON
# with the web-search tool, without changing the global model above. It must
# support tool/function calling and response_format. Keep output price within
# budget — gpt-4.1-nano is ~$0.40 / 1M output tokens. Falls back to the model
# chosen at /settings if unset.
OPENROUTER_MEDICATION_MODEL=openai/gpt-4.1-nano

# --- Supplementary context (optional) ---------------------------------------
# The main way to add practice notes/instructions is the in-app Notebook
# (/notebook) — it needs no config here and is used by the assistant automatically.
# These are optional EXTRA sources, reconciled automatically into canonical
# knowledge (no redeploy) as citable Sources the assistant can quote:
#
# Any direct text/markdown/JSON URLs (comma or newline separated) — a published
# note, a gist, or a file with a direct-download link.
# SUPPLEMENTARY_CONTEXT_URLS=
# Seconds to cache the above before re-fetching (default 300).
# SUPPLEMENTARY_CONTEXT_TTL=300

# Neon Postgres connection string (pooled endpoint). Used by the staff rota
# generator and the Notebook (lib/db.js) to store staff, saved rotas and notes.
# Get it from the Neon dashboard. The unpooled/Postgres/Prisma variants are optional.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# Vercel Blob — file attachments on Notebook notes (/api/notebook/attachments).
# Create a Blob store in the Vercel dashboard (Storage → Blob) and copy the
# read-write token. BLOB_STORE_ID is informational; the SDK only needs the token.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=vercel_blob_rw_...
BLOB_STORE_ID=store_...
